## Standing authorizations (author, 2026-06-11)

- Merge-review-merge cadence: merge each PR as soon as APPROVED + CI green;
  no long-lived branches (memory: feedback_merge_review_merge_cadence).
- Override mode: prose changes implementing the author's reading-1 briefs
  merge WITHOUT pre-merge author blessing; the author's reading-2 of the
  merged PDF is the review. Genuine NEW judgment calls (not covered by a
  brief) stay needs-human.
- Review battery per PR: parallel reviewers on a different model than the
  coder + exit-criteria gate, then merge (today's #969/#971/#972 pattern).

## Constraints

- One executor per ticket, isolated worktree, ticket as sole input.
- Sequential merges; rebase onto origin/main at every gate.
- House rules: tests/test_manuscript_crossref.py (no hand-typed numbers),
  zero-prose-drift evidence for mechanical passes, erg close in the PR.
- After the wave: rebuild slides/manuscript/main.pdf on the primary checkout
  for the author's reading-2; report which annotation items were waived.

